Step 4: Create Secure Postgres RPC Verification Functions
Write secure database RPC functions (SECURITY DEFINER) that take the activation input parameters, check the correct pre-approved role table internally on the backend, and return a secure match status.

We will open the SQL Editor in your Supabase dashboard and run a SQL script to create secure PostgreSQL RPC functions (SECURITY DEFINER).
Each function will take the activation credentials provided by the user, internally check the correct pre-approved whitelist table on the backend while bypassing RLS restrictions safely, and return a secure match status. This allows the frontend to verify staff credentials without exposing raw table data or direct queries to the browser.

we pasted this to sql editor and ran it it was successful:

-- 1. RPC function to verify pre-approved admin
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION verify_pre_approved_admin(
    p_email VARCHAR,
    p_temppass VARCHAR,
    p_initials VARCHAR,
    p_firstname VARCHAR,
    p_surname VARCHAR,
    p_phone VARCHAR
)
RETURNS BOOLEAN
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
BEGIN
    RETURN EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM pre_approved_admins
        WHERE email = p_email
          AND temppass = p_temppass
          AND initials = p_initials
          AND firstname = p_firstname
          AND surname = p_surname
          AND phone = p_phone
    );
END;
$$;

-- 2. RPC function to verify pre-approved academic head
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION verify_pre_approved_academic_head(
    p_email VARCHAR,
    p_temppass VARCHAR,
    p_initials VARCHAR,
    p_firstname VARCHAR,
    p_surname VARCHAR,
    p_phone VARCHAR
)
RETURNS BOOLEAN
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
BEGIN
    RETURN EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM pre_approved_academic_heads
        WHERE email = p_email
          AND temppass = p_temppass
          AND initials = p_initials
          AND firstname = p_firstname
          AND surname = p_surname
          AND phone = p_phone
    );
END;
$$;

-- 3. RPC function to verify pre-approved system admin
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION verify_pre_approved_system_admin(
